    "recommendations": "Maintaining clear and unobstructed travel along the driveway and access road could improve response times and support effective apparatus positioning, particularly given the single point of entry. Marking or identifying the primary access point at the street frontage may assist responding units in locating the entry during low-visibility or nighttime conditions. Keeping the unpaved circulation route passable and free of encroachments would support movement around the structure and may enhance rear access options for personnel and equipment. Managing dense vegetation adjacent to travel corridors and the main building could improve responder visibility and facilitate safer movement throughout the property during emergency operations."
