    "recommendations": "Reducing fuel continuity within the areas of heavy brush and dense shrub cover near the property could meaningfully improve defensible space and reduce opportunities for fire spread toward structures. Where brush concentrations exist closest to improvements, creating separation between individual shrub groupings may reduce the likelihood of continuous flame spread across the property. The vegetated access route would benefit from ongoing management to maintain adequate clearance along both sides and overhead, which could support firefighter access and improve evacuation conditions. Given that a single access route serves the property, keeping that corridor clear of encroaching vegetation is particularly important for suppression operations and emergency response. Preserving and maintaining the existing open terrain and open fuel break as functional buffers could support long-term wildfire resilience by limiting the transition of fire from the surrounding brushland interface toward the improved areas of the property."
